  "contract": [
    "Catalog permission is checked before route selection and after credential resolution before each chat, streamed chat, embedding, or generic provider attempt. The shared attempt callback also governs retries and route fallbacks.",
    "A failed permission check stops the current attempt chain without provider-health blame. The error is retryable for a new request.",
    "Exact chat, embedding, and semantic cache hits check permission after lookup. Cached streams check again on first read and retain a refusal even if permission later recovers. An admitted stream can complete.",
    "The HTTP chat handler reads the first event before writing response headers. Both OpenAI and OpenRouter return 503 when current permission is unavailable.",
    "The successful snapshot permission check allocates zero times and performs no storage access. Existing route preparation and cache lookups have separate latency work."
  ],
